iomarker discovery"},{"text":"Computational drug discovery"},{"text":"Multi-omics"},{"text":"AI for biomedical research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI + genomics pathway"},{"type":"p","text":"A particularly strong future combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Molecular Biology","Genomics","Bioinformatics","AI"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Deep learning"},{"text":"Sequence modelling"},{"text":"Protein modelling"},{"text":"Multi-omics analysis"},{"text":"Generative AI for biology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential applications:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Variant interpretation"},{"text":"Biomarker discovery"},{"text":"Disease prediction"},{"text":"Drug discovery"},{"text":"Protein design"},{"text":"Gene-expression prediction"},{"text":"Patient stratification"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This creates pathways into computational biology and AI-for-biomedicine, in addition to traditional wet-lab research."},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046 evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Biomedical research is likely to increasingly integrate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Genomics","AI","automation","multi-omics","precision medicine"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Traditional research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Hypothesis","Experiment","Data","Analysis"]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Large-scale biological data","AI-assisted hypothesis generation","Automated experimentation","Multi-omics analysis","Experimental validation"]},{"type":"p","text":"Important technologies may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Single-cell sequencing"},{"text":"Spatial omics"},{"text":"AI protein design"},{"text":"Automated laboratories"},{"text":"CRISPR technologies"},{"text":"Digital biology"},{"text":"Multi-omics integration"},{"text":"AI drug discovery"},{"text":"Precision medicine"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The future researcher will increasingly need both wet-lab expertise and computational/statistical capability."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended final skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Biology"},{"type":"flow","items":["Cell Biology","Genetics","Molecular Biology","Biochemistry"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Laboratory"},{"type":"flow","items":["DNA/RNA extraction","PCR/qPCR","electrophoresis","protein assays","cell culture"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Genomics"},{"type":"flow","items":["NGS","variant analysis","RNA-seq","genome annotation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Bioinformatics"},{"type":"flow","items":["Linux","Python/R","Biopython","Bioconductor","Git","workflow tools"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"flow","items":["Experimental design","hypothesis testing","regression","multiple-testing concepts"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Literature review","scientific writing","reproducibility","research ethics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"flow","items":["Machine Learning","AI","Multi-omics","Computational Biology"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Medical Biotechnology / Molecular Biology / Genomics","Research Internship","Research Assistant / Junior Research Role","M.Sc Biotechnology / Molecular Biology / Genomics / Bioinformatics","Research Associate","Senior Research Associate","Research Scientist"]},{"type":"p","text":"For advanced research:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc","M.Sc","PhD","Postdoctoral/Research Scientist","Senior Scientist / Principal Investigator"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"For a Research Associate, the strongest combination is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Molecular biology","hands-on laboratory techniques","genomics","bioinformatics","statistics","scientific writing","genuine research experience."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc graduate can enter research-support positions, but “Research Associate” is not a standardised entry-level title across all organisations. For a long-term scientific career, an M.Sc is a strong next step, while a PhD is generally important for independent research leadership and many advanced scientist positions."},{"type":"p","text":"The most future-proof route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Wet-lab biology","computational genomics","statistics","AI"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"That combination allows progression across biotechnology, diagnostics, pharmaceutical R&D, biomedical research and computational biology."}]}]}